    {
      "sourceRef": "index:20",
      "cellIndex": 20,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "### Euler-Lagrange equations",
      "sourceSha256": "141410d075b5cd03f5a1902e3c667d67981b4ff1a2c3cf42d7ba4b9765a5ac24",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:21",
      "cellIndex": 21,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "def eulerLagrange(T, V, coordinateGeneralized):\n    '''    \n    Provides the Euler-Lagrange equation for one generalized coordinate starting from the energies.\n    \n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    T : Sympy Equality (sympy.core.relational.Equality)\n        The kinetic energy of the system is explicit on the right-hand side, as a function of the generalized coordinates and velocities, and time.\n    V : Igualdad Sympy (sympy.core.relational.Equality)\n        The potential energy of the system is explicit on the right-hand side, as a function of the generalized coordinates and velocities, and time.\n    coordinateGeneralized: Sympy Symbol (sympy.core.symbol.Symbol)\n        for which we are looking the Euler-Lagrange equation\n        \n    Returns\n    -------\n    Sympy Equality (sympy.core.relational.Equality)\n        Homogeneous Euler-Lagrange equation\n    '''\n    lagrangian = (T.rhs - V.rhs).expand()\n    t = sm.Symbol('t') # since we have to differentiate respect to time, the function diff declares t as a symbol\n    return sm.Eq(\n        lagrangian.diff(coordinateGeneralized) \n        - lagrangian.diff(coordinateGeneralized.diff(t)).diff(t)\n        , 0\n    ).simplify()",
      "sourceSha256": "3ac466207caa5e0b3cbdd2f3d5ee7fe536f5ed89038b44d0817cec7033f82e02",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "coordinateGeneralized.diff",
          "diff",
          "expand",
          "lagrangian.diff",
          "simplify",
          "sm.Eq",
          "sm.Symbol"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:22",
      "cellIndex": 22,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "#### For $x$",
      "sourceSha256": "2e40426a18cd35acde7186a13d652cea60b4c4485b6c2a10b1c0fe056726cc43",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "x"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:23",
      "cellIndex": 23,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_EL = eulerLagrange(T, V, x)\nx_EL",
      "sourceSha256": "59b4466c72777978ebe7981483fe4bd04280a65f3aac60d1d6da18503afe8bca",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "                  2                                     \n- \\ell⋅m₂⋅sin(φ)⋅φ̇  + \\ell⋅m₂⋅cos(φ)⋅φ̈ + m₁⋅ẍ + m₂⋅ẍ = 0",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle - \\ell m_{2} \\sin{\\left(\\phi \\right)} \\dot{\\phi}^{2} + \\ell m_{2} \\cos{\\left(\\phi \\right)} \\ddot{\\phi} + m_{1} \\ddot{x} + m_{2} \\ddot{x} = 0$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
