      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:24",
      "cellIndex": 24,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "This is an homogeneous second order linear differential equation. We can isolate $\\ddot{x}$.",
      "sourceSha256": "8e0ff60181fd168e334fecb06cc5506d7bb6fad25a853fa7a8c6de25b99df526",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\ddot{x}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:25",
      "cellIndex": 25,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "sm.Eq(x.diff(t,2),\n       list( sm.solveset(x_EL, x.diff(t,2) ) )[0]  # solveset returns a set, that we convert into a list\n      ) # acceleration = x dot dot [m s-2]",
      "sourceSha256": "918c78a43f472ccf576805a74f6af245e19a39af1288da51e981da2b93db7276",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "            ⎛        2           ⎞\n    \\ell⋅m₂⋅⎝sin(φ)⋅φ̇  - cos(φ)⋅φ̈⎠\nẍ = ──────────────────────────────\n               m₁ + m₂            ",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\ddot{x} = \\frac{\\ell m_{2} \\left(\\sin{\\left(\\phi \\right)} \\dot{\\phi}^{2} - \\cos{\\left(\\phi \\right)} \\ddot{\\phi}\\right)}{m_{1} + m_{2}}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "list",
          "sm.Eq",
          "sm.solveset",
          "x.diff"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:26",
      "cellIndex": 26,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "This result is a function of another acceleration, $\\ddot{\\phi}$.",
      "sourceSha256": "21bc9d560ae363083d05b3357769551f63d5843839206d1030c52838bfa73b3a",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\ddot{\\phi}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:27",
      "cellIndex": 27,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "#### For $\\phi$",
      "sourceSha256": "91728975ffc24814b4c5f0710d5dfb709fa9ca316936be87217c2969cda8d67f",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\phi"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:28",
      "cellIndex": 28,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "phi_EL = eulerLagrange(T, V, phi)\nphi_EL",
      "sourceSha256": "062ad4f218946d598bd23fbba2ba19c4fc492e967143ccc37e470d5aab4f5596",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "\\ell⋅m₂⋅(\\ell⋅φ̈ + g⋅sin(φ) + cos(φ)⋅ẍ) = 0",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\ell m_{2} \\left(\\ell \\ddot{\\phi} + g \\sin{\\left(\\phi \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(\\phi \\right)} \\ddot{x}\\right) = 0$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "eulerLagrange"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:29",
      "cellIndex": 29,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "Again, we could try isolating the corresponding generalized acceleration.",
      "sourceSha256": "bf06f0be21ea03b2f2a58c0d48986cfa1a4c3593a2562de8d7d787970a5561dd",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:30",
      "cellIndex": 30,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "sm.Eq(phi.diff(t,2),\n       list( sm.solveset(phi_EL, phi.diff(t,2) ) )[0]  # solveset returns a set, that we convert into a list\n      )",
      "sourceSha256": "531cb216f07ee88dde453e345974543dc1525610a41f008202f3ff0c8e71dc22",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "    -(g⋅sin(φ) + cos(φ)⋅ẍ) \nφ̈ = ───────────────────────\n              \\ell         ",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\ddot{\\phi} = - \\frac{g \\sin{\\left(\\phi \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(\\phi \\right)} \\ddot{x}}{\\ell}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "list",
          "phi.diff",
          "sm.Eq",
          "sm.solveset"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:31",
      "cellIndex": 31,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "This is also expressed as a function of another acceleration, $\\ddot{x}$.",
      "sourceSha256": "df7b924938ed43ad45e8ccf887f7ac3ff390d5067d8b5639638628b284874f8e",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\ddot{x}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:32",
      "cellIndex": 32,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Numerical solution of the Euler-Lagrange equations",
      "sourceSha256": "559c30221bbf669093cd8fbddf27a637e5897c5df578f0c9cf64afb362a6921d",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:33",
      "cellIndex": 33,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "### Solving the system of Euler-Lagrange equations",
      "sourceSha256": "56a9eb7ef45b61e01765a8a3190147f89fcd1fc24663efe8c4225502fe4e0db5",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:34",
      "cellIndex": 34,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "The state vector must hold the generalized coordinates and velocities.",
      "sourceSha256": "1b0f6563845d045c3924c1e5b373f5e09bbdc37ea097fa24c88461589aedc925",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:35",
      "cellIndex": 35,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "y = [x, x.diff(t), phi, phi.diff(t)]\ny",
      "sourceSha256": "4df4c61fb80ee7ddae75da669de3f80350c5512d99535cb7e756f02027dc5d03",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "[x, ẋ, φ, φ̇]",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\left[ x, \\  \\dot{x}, \\  \\phi, \\  \\dot{\\phi}\\right]$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "phi.diff",
          "x.diff"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:36",
      "cellIndex": 36,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "The derivative of the state vector with respect to time will hold the generalized accelerations.\nSimilar to the case of a single coordinate, the acceleration must be expressed in terms of coordinates and velocities.",
      "sourceSha256": "6dd29f76360c270a0e9611b28ee38a99c00e689a757813f00b50456677d2f3b2",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:37",
      "cellIndex": 37,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "y_p = [y_i.diff(t) for y_i in y]\ny_p",
      "sourceSha256": "68abdcba6078414ef58db76ffe3d21658c230a744c5c5e498a52f6427a850e46",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "[ẋ, ẍ, φ̇, φ̈]",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\left[ \\dot{x}, \\  \\ddot{x}, \\  \\dot{\\phi}, \\  \\ddot{\\phi}\\right]$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "y_i.diff"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:38",
      "cellIndex": 38,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "systemEquations = [\n    x_EL,\n    phi_EL,\n]\nvariablesIsolated = [x.diff(t,2), phi.diff(t,2)] # isolate the generalized accelerations\nvariablesIsolated_sol= sm.nonlinsolve(systemEquations, variablesIsolated ).args[0]",
      "sourceSha256": "4c67b9fbf8e9074372db193bdcb8dcddc43ce80937e14ad9fa3fe5c16e5f8a7b",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "phi.diff",
          "sm.nonlinsolve",
          "x.diff"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:39",
      "cellIndex": 39,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_pp = sm.Eq(variablesIsolated[0], variablesIsolated_sol.args[0] ) # [m s-2]\nphi_pp = sm.Eq(variablesIsolated[1], variablesIsolated_sol.args[1] ) # [m s-2]\nx_pp, phi_pp",
      "sourceSha256": "117e4b5e9cf9481df7ca32064870856104c13d0759762c54be95260af127a8b2",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "⎛       ⎛      2           ⎞              ⎛                2              ⎞   \n⎜    m₂⋅⎝\\ell⋅φ̇  + g⋅cos(φ)⎠⋅sin(φ)      -⎝\\ell⋅m₂⋅cos(φ)⋅φ̇  + g⋅m₁ + g⋅m₂⎠⋅\n⎜ẍ = ──────────────────────────────, φ̈ = ───────────────────────────────────\n⎜                      2                                ⎛           2   ⎞     \n⎝           m₁ + m₂⋅sin (φ)                        \\ell⋅⎝m₁ + m₂⋅sin (φ)⎠     \n\n     ⎞\nsin(φ) ⎟\n───────⎟\n     ⎟\n     ⎠",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\left( \\ddot{x} = \\frac{m_{2} \\left(\\ell \\dot{\\phi}^{2} + g \\cos{\\left(\\phi \\right)}\\right) \\sin{\\left(\\phi \\right)}}{m_{1} + m_{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\phi \\right)}}, \\  \\ddot{\\phi} = - \\frac{\\left(\\ell m_{2} \\cos{\\left(\\phi \\right)} \\dot{\\phi}^{2} + g m_{1} + g m_{2}\\right) \\sin{\\left(\\phi \\right)}}{\\ell \\left(m_{1} + m_{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\phi \\right)}\\right)}\\right)$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "sm.Eq"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:40",
      "cellIndex": 40,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "### Numerical values",
      "sourceSha256": "ea92585197cc0b28037e0c111188d9aeebdfeba2ea59d4a431b2215f3206fd10",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:41",
      "cellIndex": 41,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "g_magnitude = 9.81 # [m s-2]\nm1_magnitude = 3 # [kg]\nm2_magnitude = 1 # [kg]\nl_magnitude = 2 # [m]\nmagnitudes = {\n    g : g_magnitude,\n    m1 : m1_magnitude,\n    m2 : m2_magnitude,\n    l : l_magnitude,\n}\nx_pp_magnitudes = x_pp.subs(magnitudes) # [m s-2]\nphi_pp_magnitudes = phi_pp.subs(magnitudes) # [m s-2]\nx_pp_magnitudes, phi_pp_magnitudes",
      "sourceSha256": "0155376e4c2d5e6685fbc25e82fa15786a6db3d93387ef482d909c704af7f6f1",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "⎛    ⎛                 2⎞              ⎛          2        ⎞        ⎞\n⎜    ⎝9.81⋅cos(φ) + 2⋅φ̇ ⎠⋅sin(φ)      -⎝2⋅cos(φ)⋅φ̇  + 39.24⎠⋅sin(φ) ⎟\n⎜ẍ = ───────────────────────────, φ̈ = ──────────────────────────────⎟\n⎜               2                              ⎛   2       ⎞        ⎟\n⎝            sin (φ) + 3                     2⋅⎝sin (φ) + 3⎠        ⎠",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\left( \\ddot{x} = \\frac{\\left(9.81 \\cos{\\left(\\phi \\right)} + 2 \\dot{\\phi}^{2}\\right) \\sin{\\left(\\phi \\right)}}{\\sin^{2}{\\left(\\phi \\right)} + 3}, \\  \\ddot{\\phi} = - \\frac{\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(\\phi \\right)} \\dot{\\phi}^{2} + 39.24\\right) \\sin{\\left(\\phi \\right)}}{2 \\left(\\sin^{2}{\\left(\\phi \\right)} + 3\\right)}\\right)$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "phi_pp.subs",
          "x_pp.subs"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {
          "g_magnitude": 9.81,
          "m1_magnitude": 3,
          "m2_magnitude": 1,
          "l_magnitude": 2
        },
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:42",
      "cellIndex": 42,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "We can see that both generalized coordinates are not constant, they change with the corresponding values of generalized coordinates and their derivatives, $\\ddot{x}$ and $\\ddot{\\phi}$.\nWe need to express these as functions, $\\ddot{x}= \\ddot{x}(\\phi, \\dot{\\phi})$ and $\\ddot{\\phi} = \\ddot{\\phi}(\\phi, \\dot{\\phi})$, to perform the numerical integration. ",
      "sourceSha256": "932cd9622ba39671c345d63d0ba22c51fea69638749099b6c405706f18a00f0d",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\ddot{x}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\ddot{\\phi}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\ddot{x}= \\ddot{x}(\\phi, \\dot{\\phi})"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\ddot{\\phi} = \\ddot{\\phi}(\\phi, \\dot{\\phi})"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:43",
      "cellIndex": 43,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "### Generating functions from SymPy expressions",
      "sourceSha256": "f74362efaa5394f79de53f636fa30d210239b5a90133ee77541db942778625b0",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:44",
      "cellIndex": 44,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "The `SymPy` library has a method called `lambdify` to convert a symbolic expression into a function that takes generalized coordinates and velocities as inputs.\nWe have to define these variables explicitly.\nThese are contained in the state vector $\\vec{y}$.",
      "sourceSha256": "5ff45d32f9d36d11df7e7847a9e252f706e9c126ef1e9070341f6fd1ece9524b",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\vec{y}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:45",
      "cellIndex": 45,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "y",
      "sourceSha256": "a1fce4363854ff888cff4b8e7875d600c2682390412a8cf79b37d0b11148b0fa",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "[x, ẋ, φ, φ̇]",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\left[ x, \\  \\dot{x}, \\  \\phi, \\  \\dot{\\phi}\\right]$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:46",
      "cellIndex": 46,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_pp_lambda = sm.lambdify(y, x_pp_magnitudes.rhs) # [m s-2], y is the state vector\nphi_pp_lambda = sm.lambdify(y, phi_pp_magnitudes.rhs) # [m s-2]",
      "sourceSha256": "5acdaddb721adaa8211ccfd0f914c94e7eaf65d097485c5074163ed8e030afa0",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "sm.lambdify"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:47",
      "cellIndex": 47,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "Let's check that the new type generated by `lambdify` is a function.",
      "sourceSha256": "edd02c204a2ae8fc6d05eefa86888fe8f1fafaa8db758ad2bdf0385b113f8691",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:48",
      "cellIndex": 48,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "type(x_pp_lambda), type(x_pp_magnitudes.rhs)",
      "sourceSha256": "8267d02e03b14f8164e17b91081ddf5524d5064561cba2be00e3d4a7ace34900",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "(function, sympy.core.mul.Mul)"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "type"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:49",
      "cellIndex": 49,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "### Initial conditions\nNow we set the initial conditions and the range for times.",
      "sourceSha256": "2427476e831b557958b8728f1547802bb1efd40dc136e7522f116d9c9dfe2974",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:50",
      "cellIndex": 50,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "# library for numerical analysis\nimport numpy as np",
      "sourceSha256": "b26e388d1548553d8d7d74d8d226f441aa62377b4d294828950f5f6db9ac2a45",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [
          "numpy"
        ],
        "calls": [],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:51",
      "cellIndex": 51,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "# if we need a number such as Pi, it must be from numpy\ny_initial = [1, 0.5, np.pi/8, 0\n            ] # [SI units] ordered for the state vector\nt_range = np.linspace(0, 10, 100) # initial and final times, and how many intermediate values.",
      "sourceSha256": "97b5f07d96f03544fb3cbe96de582fe3d2a247182e7e67c52ed4c950f0190b47",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "np.linspace"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:52",
      "cellIndex": 52,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "We integrate through the steps in `t_range`.\n\n> Reference:\n> - https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/tutorial/integrate.html",
      "sourceSha256": "eefbdc725c341f29fa3ae4077d7ba1306871c483c4990599b6951b874fc5d46a",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:53",
      "cellIndex": 53,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "# library for scientific calculations: efficient tools for numerical analysis\n# We import the function solve_ivp: it solves a system of ODEs with initial conditions.\n# https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.integrate.solve_ivp.html#scipy.integrate.solve_ivp\nfrom scipy.integrate import solve_ivp",
      "sourceSha256": "d58e0daf73b361a3ca87df7e0ac85ab5f734b016d7b4320e56b2933b67fe1624",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [
          "scipy.integrate"
        ],
        "calls": [],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:54",
      "cellIndex": 54,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "# we define a function con the system of derivatives\n# t : it's not used in this system, but we leave for a later use\n# y : list of states with [y[0], y[1], y[2], y[3]]\n# y[0]: x\n# y[1]: x dot\n# y[2]: phi\n# y[3]: phi dot\n# dydt : list of derivatives\ndef y_dot(t, y):\n    dydt = [y[1],\n            x_pp_lambda(y[0], y[1], y[2], y[3]),\n            y[3],\n            phi_pp_lambda(y[0], y[1], y[2], y[3]),\n           ]\n    return dydt",
      "sourceSha256": "a7fa9acb4530a5bac48a5732b29ef4673155ef1e1c8bf25d3f732f1218892df6",
